<section class="or-section or-paper" id="or-faq">
  <div class="or-wrap">
    <div class="or-faq-layout">

      <div class="or-faq-intro">
        <span class="or-eyebrow">Product Questions</span>
        <h2 class="or-heading">Surface Mount Push Operators FAQs</h2>
        <div class="or-line"></div>
        <p>
          Information about the OA100 push operator range,
          available configurations, technical specifications
          and product documentation.
        </p>
        <a class="or-text-link" href="https://omegaautomatics.com/contact">
          Ask Omega a Question →
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="or-faq-list">

        <details class="or-faq-item">
          <summary>What is a surface mount push door operator?</summary>
          <p>
            It is an automatic swing door operator installed
            above the door in a surface-mounted arrangement.
            A push-arm configuration is used to push the
            door panel open.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="or-faq-item">
          <summary>Which models are available in the OA100 push series?</summary>
          <p>
            The published model range includes PS-L, PS-R,
            PS-AA, PS-AM and PS-MA.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="or-faq-item">
          <summary>Does the series support single and dual doors?</summary>
          <p>
            Yes. The listed model range includes left-hand
            and right-hand single-door arrangements as well
            as dual-door configurations.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="or-faq-item">
          <summary>What is the maximum published door capacity?</summary>
          <p>
            The product specifications list a door capacity
            of up to 450 lbs. Confirm project suitability
            with Omega before specifying the operator.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="or-faq-item">
          <summary>What power supply does the operator require?</summary>
          <p>
            The published power supply is 120VAC, 60Hz.
            The product also lists an on-board 24VDC,
            1.2A power supply.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="or-faq-item">
          <summary>What are the standard header lengths?</summary>
          <p>
            The standard header lengths are 39" and 41".
            Custom lengths are available on request.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="or-faq-item">
          <summary>What does PS-AA mean?</summary>
          <p>
            PS-AA is the dual active/active push operator
            configuration listed in the product range.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="or-faq-item">
          <summary>What are PS-AM and PS-MA configurations?</summary>
          <p>
            PS-AM represents an active/manual arrangement,
            while PS-MA represents a manual/active arrangement.
            Refer to the respective drawings for model details.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="or-faq-item">
          <summary>Can the opening and closing speeds be adjusted?</summary>
          <p>
            Yes. Adjustable opening and closing speeds are
            included in the published key features.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="or-faq-item">
          <summary>Does the OA100 push operator include Push & Go?</summary>
          <p>
            Push & Go is listed as a selectable feature
            in the product information.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="or-faq-item">
          <summary>Which finish options are available?</summary>
          <p>
            The two published options are anodized clear
            and anodized black finishes.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="or-faq-item">
          <summary>Does the operator support electric locks?</summary>
          <p>
            The specifications list an electric lock input
            with fail-safe and fail-secure options.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="or-faq-item">
          <summary>What is the published temperature range?</summary>
          <p>
            The product information lists an operating
            temperature range of -30°C to +50°C.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="or-faq-item">
          <summary>Is a magnetic position reader included?</summary>
          <p>
            Yes. The published specifications list an
            included magnetic position reader.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="or-faq-item">
          <summary>Where can I find the technical drawings?</summary>
          <p>
            Model-specific PDF drawings for PS-L, PS-R,
            PS-AA, PS-AM and PS-MA are available in the
            Technical Resources section of this page.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="or-faq-item">
          <summary>What warranty is listed for the product?</summary>
          <p>
            The published product page lists a one-year
            parts warranty from the date of invoice.
          </p>
        </details>

